Choose the factor to arrange $$\label{eq:normalization}
 m=((n+1)c)^{-n}<s_n,
 \qquad cq_0m^{1/n}=\frac1n.$$

$$\label{chord:normalization}
 0<W:=\int_Y v^p\,d\mu<s_n,\qquad Q(v)=nW,
 \qquad \,d\nu=\frac{v^p}{W}\,d\mu.$$ The last expression defines a probability measure. By Lemma <a href="#lem:powers" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="lem:powers">21</a>, $v$ has all finite positive moments and $$\label{chord:weighted-energy}
 \int_Y v^q\lvert Dv\rvert^2\,d\mu<\infty\qquad(q\ge0).$$ Choose a finite nonnegative Borel representative of $v$; changing it on a $\mu$-null set has no effect on these assertions.

